From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: Keys that toggle in the in-game menu of a game's own app

A game's own app has no touch layout editor, so its in-game menu gets
"Keys that toggle": the single keys (A B X Y, L R ZL ZR, L3 R3, minus,
plus) with a checkmark each. A pick applies at once and is saved as
launcher.DM_TOUCH_TOGGLE, which the next start reads when the environment
has no DM_TOUCH_TOGGLE. It also sets DM_TOUCH_TOGGLE in the process, so
both ways hold the same value. The shared app keeps its layout editor and
shows no entry (dm_shell_return_to_library is linked there). A key that
stops toggling is released.

Tests: pad_geometry_check.m (dm_pad_toggle_encode reads back, skips what
cannot toggle).

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on the touch patches 0065 to 0070 and 0090, forwarded once those land upstream]
Reason: Touch keys that toggle in a game's own app, which has no layout editor
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#658
